From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VirusBurst <VirusBurst@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:13:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: h616: dram: select rank 1 in the second read-training
 pass

mctl_phy_read_training() runs a second pass for dual-rank setups, but
writes the same rank selector (2) to PHY register 0x198[1:0] as the
first pass, so rank 0 is trained twice and rank 1 never. The source
already carried a "maybe last parameter should be 1?" comment.

All other per-rank steps in this driver use 2 for rank 0 and 1 for
rank 1:
 - write leveling:   PHY 0x08[7:6]  = 2 / 1
 - read calibration: PHY 0x08[5:4]  = 2 / 1
 - write training:   PHY 0x198[3:2] = 2 / 1
so use 1 for the rank-1 read-training pass as well.

This only has an effect on dual-rank boards that enable read training
(TPR10 bit 22, TPR10_READ_TRAINING). Among the in-tree H616 defconfigs
only orangepi_zero2_defconfig sets that bit, and its DDR3 is single
rank, so it is not affected. The X96Q Plus configuration does not set
bit 22 either; the fix is therefore build-tested, and boot-tested only
with read training disabled. The same pattern exists in
dram_sun55i_a523.c and is left untouched here.

Assisted-by: Grok
Signed-off-by: VirusBurst <VirusBurst@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
index b73d51a3..d12282a2 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
@@ -536,8 +536,14 @@ static bool mctl_phy_read_training(const struct dram_para *para,
 	clrbits_le32(SUNXI_DRAM_PHY0_BASE + 0x190, 3);
 
 	if (config->ranks == 2) {
-		/* maybe last parameter should be 1? */
-		clrsetbits_le32(SUNXI_DRAM_PHY0_BASE + 0x198, 3, 2);
+		/*
+		 * Select rank 1. Rank 0 uses 2 here; the other per-rank
+		 * training steps use the same encoding (write training:
+		 * 0x198[3:2] = 2 for rank 0 and 1 for rank 1, read
+		 * calibration: 0x8[5:4] = 2/1, write leveling 0x8[7:6] = 2/1),
+		 * so writing 2 again only re-trained rank 0.
+		 */
+		clrsetbits_le32(SUNXI_DRAM_PHY0_BASE + 0x198, 3, 1);
 
 		setbits_le32(SUNXI_DRAM_PHY0_BASE + 0x190, 6);
 		setbits_le32(SUNXI_DRAM_PHY0_BASE + 0x190, 1);
